00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.780
Starship V3, upper stage, changes at pad 2, expose the exact hardware limits that must be solved before the first orbital flight can succeed. This is SpaceX Daily, episode 91. Revised tanking sequences and structural interfaces altered load paths on the ship upper stage during recent V3 testing at the upgraded launch mount. Engineers traced the problems to tighter thermal margins required by the larger propellant loads. Yesterday's test data showed the ship stage

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:41.520
experiencing unexpected stress concentrations at the interstage connection points. Further ground testing will focus on confirming that the updated thermal protection layout maintains margins during ascent.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:56.180
The analysis highlights how these fixes must close before the vehicle can attempt full orbital velocity. This builds on the ongoing flight test campaign at starbase by identifying specific limits in the upper stage before orbital attempts.

