Next step center on revalidating the integrated pad systems with the revised hardware stack. Blue origin is adding new test stands and launch infrastructure at Kennedy Space Center and Cape Canaveral. The expansion includes dedicated pads for its new Glenn vehicle and supporting ground equipment. Multiple sites are being prepared in parallel to increased test cadence. The moves position the company to conduct more frequent static fires and flight tests from Florida facilities.

