Open AI's decision to cut cursors access to its models has strengthened arguments for open source alternatives that avoid similar vendor restrictions.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:18.020
From an engineering standpoint the decision to cast and finish its own turbine blades for Raptor engines starts from a simple materials constraint.

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:22.840
The blades must survive extreme temperatures and stresses while adding minimal mass.

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:35.200
Raw nickel-based super alloy stock is relatively inexpensive yet finished blades have historically carried large markups because of complex external supply chains and proprietary forming processes.

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:47.020
By bringing casting machining and coding steps inside its own facilities space X collapses the idiot index through direct control of every variable from grain structure to cooling channel geometry.

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:56.080
The internal process also lets engineers adjust blade root fillets and tip shrouds without waiting for supplier requalification cycles.

00:07:56.760 --> 00:08:01.180
The approach shortens the feedback loop between design iteration and test hardware.

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:10.420
When a blade geometry change improves creep resistance or reduces cooling flow the new version can be produced and evaluated in weeks rather than months.

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:19.300
This speed matters because Raptor thrust and specific impulse gains depend on incremental improvements across hundreds of individual blades per engine.

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:26.160
Faster iteration directly supports the higher engine production rates required for starships target flight cadence.

00:08:26.780 --> 00:08:35.520
In practice the first in-house blade batches have already completed more than 200 hot fire seconds with no measurable erosion beyond predicted limits.

00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:48.820
The same logic extends to quality control internal production allows statistical process control on every heat and every coding batch reducing the chance that a single supplier deviation grounds an entire vehicle.

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:57.860
Over time the cost per blade trends toward the true materials and energy floor rather than the previous market price inflated by margins and lead times.

00:08:58.460 --> 00:09:03.040
That compression is what ultimately makes the engine economics viable for rapid reuse.

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:13.180
The next visible milestone will be whether the in-house blades maintain performance through the full 1000 second life target now set for Raptor 3 qualification units.

